# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store

# --- Heavy source material (sources/) ---
# The manufacturer PDFs and the .xlsx halves of the source-extract registers
# live in the working tree but stay out of git: factory/ alone is ~438 MB.
# The .md halves of every register ARE tracked - they are the readable,
# diffable version of the same data.
#
# Anyone cloning this repo gets sources/ as a near-empty skeleton and must
# obtain the catalog PDFs separately. Per the Object Contract, the source PDF
# is the authority, so it must never be reconstructed from git.
sources/**/*.pdf
sources/**/*.xlsx
sources/**/*.xls

# --- SketchUp scratch ---
*.skb
sources/**/*.png
sources/**/*.jpg
sources/**/*.jpeg

# --- probe reports: measurements, not data. Regenerated by the probes in tools/. ---
tools/*_report.txt

# --- build/: scratch, EXCEPT the one script that is a tool ---
# .rbz archives are made from the tree and never edited: tools/build_rbz.rb
# rebuilds them from src/ in one command, so a stale one in git is worse than
# none - it installs cleanly and then misbehaves. Same for the throwaway probe
# scripts and for commit-msg.txt, which holds the NEXT message and would sit one
# commit stale in history forever.
#
# NARROWED 2026-08-28. The rule used to be `build/` and its reason was only ever
# about ARCHIVES - a rule wider than the reason printed above it, which is the
# exact shape this project catches everywhere else. The cost showed up the first
# time Andriy opened the laptop: `sh build/go.sh` is the one command he types,
# on every machine, and it was not in the repository at all. It is a TOOL, and
# a tool travels.
build/*
!build/go.sh

# --- probe bridge: a post box into the open model, dev only ---
tools/probe_inbox/
tools/probe_outbox.txt
tools/probe_log.txt
